---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/global/Nav.astro";
import AnnouncementBar from "../components/global/AnnouncementBar.astro";
import FooterV2 from "../components/global/FooterV2.astro";
import LegalPage from "../components/legal/LegalPage.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy — VistIQ";
const description =
  "How VistIQ collects, uses, shares and protects personal data across its website and platform, and the rights you can exercise over your data.";

/** Bump when the document changes — it drives the "Last updated" line. */
const UPDATED = "2026-08-20";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="/privacy-policy"
>
  <main class="main-wrapper">
    <AnnouncementBar />
    <Nav belowAnnouncement />

    <LegalPage
      heading="Privacy Policy"
      intro="This policy explains what personal data VistIQ collects, why we collect it, who we share it with, and how you can exercise your rights."
      updated={UPDATED}
    >
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website and the VistIQ platform are operated by <span
          class="legal_placeholder">[LEGAL ENTITY NAME]</span
        >, a <span class="legal_placeholder">[LEGAL FORM]</span> registered at <span
          class="legal_placeholder">[REGISTERED ADDRESS]</span
        >, registered under number <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[COMPANY REGISTRATION NUMBER]</span
        > ("VistIQ", "we", "us").
      </p>
      <p>
        For the purposes of the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR),
        VistIQ acts as the <strong>data controller</strong> for personal data collected
        through this website and for the account data of our customers. When we process
        content that our customers upload into the platform, we act as a <strong
          >data processor</strong
        > on their behalf, under the terms of the applicable customer agreement.
      </p>
      <p>
        Data protection contact: <a href="mailto:[PRIVACY EMAIL]"
          ><span class="legal_placeholder">[PRIVACY EMAIL]</span></a
        >. <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[IF APPOINTED: DPO NAME AND CONTACT DETAILS]</span
        >
      </p>

      <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
      <h3>2.1 Data you give us</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact and demo requests</strong> — first and last name, business
          email, company name, company type, role and any message you write in our
          forms.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Account data</strong> — the identifiers and profile details needed
          to create and administer a platform account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Customer content</strong> — documents, notes and other material
          our customers upload to the platform, which may incidentally contain personal
          data about third parties.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Correspondence</strong> — the content of emails and support requests
          you send us.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2.2 Data we collect automatically</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical data</strong> — IP address, browser type and version,
          device type, operating system, language and referring page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Usage data</strong> — pages viewed, time on page and interactions
          with the site, collected in aggregate.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Security logs</strong> — records of authentication attempts and
          activity used to detect abuse.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not knowingly collect data from children, and the site is not
        directed at them.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Why we use your data, and on what legal basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>To respond to your enquiries and schedule demos</strong> — necessary
          for steps taken at your request prior to entering a contract, or our legitimate
          interest in answering business enquiries.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To provide and operate the platform</strong> — performance of the
          contract with our customer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To secure our services</strong> — our legitimate interest in preventing
          fraud, abuse and unauthorised access.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To improve the site and our products</strong> — our legitimate interest
          in understanding how our services are used, using aggregated data wherever
          possible.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To send commercial communications</strong> — your consent where
          required, or our legitimate interest in contacting business prospects.
          You can opt out at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To meet legal obligations</strong> — compliance with accounting,
          tax and other applicable law.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>
        <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[CONFIRM THE EXACT COOKIE SET IN USE BEFORE PUBLISHING]</span
        > We use strictly necessary cookies to make the site work. Where we use analytics
        or marketing cookies, we ask for your consent first and you can withdraw
        it at any time through the cookie settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most browsers let you block or delete cookies. Blocking strictly
        necessary cookies may prevent parts of the site from working.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data. We share it only with the categories of
        recipients below, under contracts that restrict what they may do with
        it:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Service providers</strong> — hosting, infrastructure, email delivery,
          analytics, CRM and support tooling. <span class="legal_placeholder"
            >[LIST KEY SUB-PROCESSORS OR LINK TO A SUB-PROCESSOR PAGE]</span
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Professional advisers</strong> — auditors, lawyers and insurers
          where necessary.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Authorities</strong> — where we are legally required to disclose
          data, or to establish or defend legal claims.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Acquirers</strong> — if we are involved in a merger, acquisition
          or asset sale, subject to the protections in this policy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Where personal data is transferred outside the European Economic Area, we
        rely on an adequacy decision or on the European Commission's Standard
        Contractual Clauses, together with any supplementary measures required.
        You can request a copy of the relevant safeguards using the contact
        details above. <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[CONFIRM HOSTING REGIONS AND TRANSFER MECHANISMS]</span
        >
      </p>

      <h2>7. How long we keep data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Enquiry and demo data</strong> — <span class="legal_placeholder"
            >[RETENTION PERIOD, e.g. 3 YEARS FROM LAST CONTACT]</span
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Account data</strong> — for the life of the account, then <span
            class="legal_placeholder">[RETENTION PERIOD]</span
          > after closure.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Customer content</strong> — for the term of the customer agreement,
          then deleted or returned per that agreement.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Accounting records</strong> — for the period required by law.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. How we protect data</h2>
      <p>
        We apply technical and organisational measures appropriate to the risk,
        including encryption in transit and at rest, access control on a
        need-to-know basis, logging and monitoring, and supplier due diligence.
        No system is completely secure, but we work to keep our safeguards
        current. <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[REFERENCE ANY CERTIFICATIONS SUCH AS SOC 2 OR ISO 27001 ONCE HELD]</span
        >
      </p>

      <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to the conditions in applicable law, you may request access to
        your personal data, its rectification or erasure, restriction of or
        objection to processing, and data portability. Where processing is based
        on consent, you may withdraw it at any time without affecting processing
        carried out beforehand.
      </p>
      <p>
        To exercise these rights, write to <a href="mailto:[PRIVACY EMAIL]"
          ><span class="legal_placeholder">[PRIVACY EMAIL]</span></a
        >. We reply within one month, and may ask you to verify your identity. If
        our answer does not satisfy you, you can lodge a complaint with your
        local supervisory authority — in France, the <a
          href="https://www.cnil.fr"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">CNIL</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your data was uploaded to the platform by one of our customers,
        address your request to that customer; we will assist them in responding.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy to reflect changes in our services or in the
        law. The revision date at the top of the page always shows the current
        version, and we will flag material changes where required.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to <a
          href="mailto:[PRIVACY EMAIL]"
          ><span class="legal_placeholder">[PRIVACY EMAIL]</span></a
        > or through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </LegalPage>

    <FooterV2 />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // Baseline only: static prose, no section animation and no reveal guard.
  import { initBaseline } from "../scripts/baseline";
  initBaseline();
</script>
